  "body": "The example describes a time 23,045 microseconds after 01:00 UTC, but the corresponding ISO timestamp is `2000-01-01T00:00:00.023045Z`.\n\nChange `01:00 UTC` to `00:00 UTC` so the starting time agrees with the ISO timestamps and the example correctly illustrates truncation to millisecond precision.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13091/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 1:48 AM UTC (1556f72)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13091/a044232...1556f72/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 1:48 AM UTC (1556f72)\">diff</a> )",
